id: pm-hfqju5
title: "GH-975: export isAlreadyClaimedError through a supported SDK subpath"
description: "Track GitHub issue #975: the shipped claim typings declare the sanctioned lost-race predicate, but no package export exposes it, forcing extensions to hard-code the internal already_claimed_by error code."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: concurrency,github,package-exports,sdk
created_at: "2026-08-11T08:33:49.248Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-11T16:25:26.366Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-11T16:21:47.737Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-11T16:21:47.737Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Export isAlreadyClaimedError from the canonical SDK lifecycle surface; packed ESM and TypeScript consumers can import it; public-surface and package-boundary gates cover the export; no extension must duplicate the internal code predicate
parent: pm-doxj
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
environment: @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.10 packed consumer
repro_steps: "Import sdk, sdk/core, and sdk/runtime from the packed package and inspect isAlreadyClaimedError; direct sdk/lifecycle/claim import is rejected by package exports."
resolution: Exported a bundle-safe isAlreadyClaimedError predicate from the supported SDK and SDK core entrypoints.
expected_result: "The documented predicate is reachable from a supported SDK subpath beside claim/release, with runtime/type/public-surface parity."
actual_result: "Packed ESM and strict TypeScript consumers import the predicate successfully, and it recognizes the canonical cross-bundle PmCliError shape without accepting unrelated errors."
component: SDK lifecycle exports
customer_impact: Extension concurrency guards couple to an internal error code and may fail open after an error-code rename.
